01:24:49.660 --> 01:24:51.420
this year and

01:24:51.740 --> 01:24:53.500
I kind of gave up in frustration.

01:24:56.095 --> 01:24:58.334
Attorney Mark Branch offered to

01:24:58.895 --> 01:25:01.615
take a cut at it that I've been

01:25:03.695 --> 01:25:06.975
mulling over for the last month or so, and

01:25:07.280 --> 01:25:11.680
I'm still not real happy with it. It comes down to

01:25:12.880 --> 01:25:14.160
an issue of

01:25:14.880 --> 01:25:16.400
political signs.

01:25:17.760 --> 01:25:18.160
Apparently,

01:25:19.985 --> 01:25:26.625
we have to allow political signs to be as big as any other sign that we have

01:25:26.865 --> 01:25:28.385
in our regulations.

01:25:29.745 --> 01:25:33.665
And we can put no restrictions on them as far as how many or how

01:25:33.825 --> 01:25:36.720
long they're up, and all that kind of stuff.

01:25:38.720 --> 01:25:39.360
And

01:25:40.320 --> 01:25:48.480
it just doesn't seem right to me that we should be able to put a political sign as big as a sign that we would have

01:25:48.725 --> 01:25:50.245
in a shopping mall

01:25:51.045 --> 01:25:52.805
or something like that. And

01:25:54.725 --> 01:25:55.365
so

01:25:55.925 --> 01:25:57.845
I'm still trying to

01:25:59.925 --> 01:26:03.285
wrestle with are there any lines of demarcation

01:26:03.365 --> 01:26:03.765
there?

01:26:07.680 --> 01:26:08.640
Anyhow,

01:26:08.880 --> 01:26:12.480
Abby, if you've got me allowed to share my screen.

01:26:20.865 --> 01:26:23.585
>> There you go. You should be able to know. Okay.

01:26:24.625 --> 01:26:25.345
>> And

01:26:30.145 --> 01:26:33.105
I'm going to try to go through with the commission because it's,

01:26:33.730 --> 01:26:39.010
you know, we're not late. I was hoping we would be and it would give me a good excuse to not do this.

01:26:39.490 --> 01:26:44.130
But we'll start working our way through some of the things that I do think we can talk about

01:26:48.775 --> 01:26:54.615
and get that out of the way so we get down to the more meaty issues after I've had another opportunity to

01:26:55.255 --> 01:26:59.415
discuss it with Mark Branch and maybe we'd have him come to

01:27:00.615 --> 01:27:01.735
a meeting to

01:27:01.975 --> 01:27:07.249
help answer questions and that sort of thing. But if I start from

01:27:07.570 --> 01:27:08.930
the top here,

01:27:10.290 --> 01:27:11.330
on intent,

01:27:12.290 --> 01:27:13.890
we just added the comment,

01:27:15.410 --> 01:27:18.450
while ensuring constitutional right of free speech is

01:27:19.265 --> 01:27:20.145
protected,

01:27:20.305 --> 01:27:28.225
I guess we got to get rid of, we got two welfares in a row there, that's a typo and we get rid of that. But that's what we're trying to do is make sure that

01:27:30.065 --> 01:27:31.345
we do not

01:27:33.220 --> 01:27:39.060
infringe on anybody's constitutional right of free speech. What that really means is that

01:27:39.860 --> 01:27:46.580
the sign is a sign, we can regulate what the size of the sign is, but we can't regulate what goes on the sign.

01:27:49.545 --> 01:27:51.625
Moving down to sign functions,

01:27:51.865 --> 01:27:52.585
you know,

01:27:53.545 --> 01:27:54.985
we were looking at

01:27:55.385 --> 01:27:57.945
sign functions before we had a

01:27:58.505 --> 01:28:01.320
multitude of different kinds of signs.

01:28:02.120 --> 01:28:04.280
I couldn't tell the difference between

01:28:04.600 --> 01:28:06.200
several of the signs

01:28:06.360 --> 01:28:07.160
and

01:28:10.440 --> 01:28:14.840
I went out and I would look at a sign and say, well, what bucket does this sign fit in?

01:28:15.725 --> 01:28:17.645
And I couldn't figure that out either.

01:28:18.285 --> 01:28:20.845
And so we've combined

01:28:21.645 --> 01:28:23.725
the sign functions

01:28:23.805 --> 01:28:25.004
into three

01:28:25.965 --> 01:28:26.765
different

01:28:27.645 --> 01:28:31.490
ones for our definition. And the first one's identification.

01:28:34.530 --> 01:28:38.850
And you can read the words there, I'm not going to read them out loud, but

01:28:39.330 --> 01:28:46.254
does anybody have any comments on those specific words? I think those words are probably okay

01:28:46.255 --> 01:28:46.975
and

01:28:47.295 --> 01:28:48.415
that covers

01:28:48.735 --> 01:28:51.215
a bunch of our signs identifying what

01:28:51.855 --> 01:28:54.175
the business commodity or service is.

01:28:54.335 --> 01:28:55.295
That's

01:28:55.295 --> 01:28:56.095
what that one does.

01:28:57.800 --> 01:29:00.280
That's one of the three buckets that we're gonna

01:29:01.240 --> 01:29:02.440
end up talking about.

01:29:04.040 --> 01:29:08.840
The next one is the billboard. We didn't want to prohibit it in the definition,

01:29:08.840 --> 01:29:10.360
we'll prohibit that later on,

01:29:11.345 --> 01:29:15.505
but we're saying a billboard would be a sign with a face

01:29:15.665 --> 01:29:22.545
in excess of 32 square feet. And again, 32 square feet is your basic four by eight sheet of plywood, which I thought,

01:29:23.270 --> 01:29:27.990
there's a lot of signs that go up that are made out of a sheet of plywood and anything

01:29:27.990 --> 01:29:30.150
bigger than that's a billboard, then

01:29:32.230 --> 01:29:33.910
that's the definition of that.

01:29:34.950 --> 01:29:38.470
So that's only up there so that we can prohibit it later on.

01:29:39.985 --> 01:29:42.945
The second category is a temporary sign.

01:29:47.425 --> 01:29:48.385
And again,

01:29:49.745 --> 01:29:51.025
the words all look good.

01:29:51.810 --> 01:29:55.810
This is where we do talk about a political sign

01:29:56.130 --> 01:29:59.490
being in the temporary sign bucket.

01:30:01.090 --> 01:30:03.090
And I guess at the end of the day,

01:30:03.810 --> 01:30:06.850
my thought would be a temporary sign doesn't need a permit,

01:30:07.365 --> 01:30:10.965
a permanent sign does need a permit. It could be just that easy,

01:30:11.365 --> 01:30:13.445
but I haven't figured out how to make it

01:30:13.845 --> 01:30:17.845
that easy in the writing of the regs yet, but that's where I'm trying to go.

01:30:20.405 --> 01:30:21.525
All these things,

01:30:21.765 --> 01:30:22.725
know, tag sale,

01:30:23.800 --> 01:30:25.720
steak fry at the firehouse,

01:30:26.360 --> 01:30:27.720
political signs,

01:30:29.080 --> 01:30:31.560
and a political sign includes

01:30:32.360 --> 01:30:35.320
those signs that say unmask our kids,

01:30:35.965 --> 01:30:37.325
Black Lives Matter,

01:30:37.405 --> 01:30:44.525
all those kinds of things that have a political slant to them are the political signs where we can't really put too much

01:30:44.925 --> 01:30:46.125
restriction on.

01:30:46.925 --> 01:30:47.405
And so

01:30:48.310 --> 01:30:51.350
one of the things I need to come through with Markbratz is,

01:30:51.910 --> 01:30:53.430
are you telling me that

01:30:54.470 --> 01:30:56.310
the sign at the Extramart

01:30:56.310 --> 01:31:02.405
looks to me to be higher than 10 feet and bigger than 32 feet, and that's what our

01:31:02.805 --> 01:31:04.325
regulations require.

01:31:04.325 --> 01:31:04.725
And

01:31:05.445 --> 01:31:06.885
you know, how can that be?

01:31:07.445 --> 01:31:10.885
Something's not in sync with our regulations at that point yet, I'm trying to figure that out.

01:31:12.660 --> 01:31:19.780
But we all know what a temporary sign is, that's what you bang onto the tree, you put in the ground announcing your tag sale,

01:31:20.020 --> 01:31:22.180
announcing your political

01:31:22.180 --> 01:31:23.460
candidates,

01:31:23.700 --> 01:31:24.500
all that kind of stuff,

01:31:25.315 --> 01:31:27.235
the bake sale at the school,

01:31:27.875 --> 01:31:29.955
you name it, that's a temporary sign.

01:31:32.115 --> 01:31:42.280
We got rid of a bunch more public interest sign. This is what I thought, you know, going through it used, I thought this was anything that was of interest to the public.

01:31:43.480 --> 01:31:45.160
But these are the signs

01:31:45.240 --> 01:31:49.720
that the town or the state or the federal government posts.

01:31:50.440 --> 01:31:52.725
And they, you know, speed limit signs,

01:31:53.045 --> 01:31:54.725
no passing signs.

01:31:56.565 --> 01:32:00.245
We've got signs that, you know, at the corner of 316

01:32:00.245 --> 01:32:01.045
and

01:32:02.965 --> 01:32:08.640
School Road that show this, the firehouse, the school, town hall.

01:32:09.200 --> 01:32:12.480
We've got signs for Hearst Farm that the town has put up.

01:32:13.120 --> 01:32:15.840
All those kinds of things are public interest signs.

01:32:16.255 --> 01:32:18.895
And that's the third bucket that we'd be in.

01:32:19.375 --> 01:32:20.575
And so I think

01:32:21.295 --> 01:32:25.615
public interest signs are permanent, identification signs are permanent,

01:32:25.775 --> 01:32:27.455
and temporary signs are temporary.

01:32:29.080 --> 01:32:31.480
And it was going to be just that easy.

01:32:31.800 --> 01:32:33.720
So anybody have

01:32:35.640 --> 01:32:36.360
any

01:32:36.920 --> 01:32:39.000
comments on that little bit?

01:32:41.255 --> 01:32:42.535
>> I

01:32:43.895 --> 01:32:49.415
have a question for you on that. Have other towns used this three bucket approach

01:32:49.655 --> 01:32:51.895
or would this be unique to Andover?

01:32:52.375 --> 01:32:53.975
>> It's unique

01:32:53.975 --> 01:32:54.695
to Andover.

01:32:56.650 --> 01:32:57.770
I

01:32:57.770 --> 01:33:00.010
have looked at a couple of other towns

01:33:00.810 --> 01:33:04.890
and I've not been happy with theirs either. This recent

01:33:08.730 --> 01:33:09.610
thing about

01:33:11.165 --> 01:33:13.645
free speech and signs is,

01:33:16.125 --> 01:33:21.165
I haven't seen a good example out there that I was happy with and wanted to use.

01:33:21.325 --> 01:33:24.605
And if you get The Hartford Courant, there was

01:33:24.970 --> 01:33:30.090
a copy of, well, there was a story, I think it was on the front page, where

01:33:31.690 --> 01:33:34.090
the ribbons around trees

01:33:34.170 --> 01:33:37.050
in some town in the Northwest side of the state

01:33:37.875 --> 01:33:39.635
was the big political

01:33:39.635 --> 01:33:41.075
to do. Somebody

01:33:41.475 --> 01:33:47.235
for Veterans Day wanted to put yellow ribbons around the trees for honoring the veterans.

01:33:47.795 --> 01:33:51.360
The town said no, because, you know, if

01:33:51.440 --> 01:33:56.880
we allow that, then we'd have to allow all these different colors of ribbons around trees and

01:33:57.120 --> 01:33:59.920
they weren't going there. So everybody's wrestling with

01:34:00.640 --> 01:34:02.880
the political ramifications

01:34:02.880 --> 01:34:08.885
of this, but I haven't seen anything I like better than what we're trying to do. And we're

01:34:08.885 --> 01:34:12.005
trying to build on the lessons learned from other towns

01:34:13.365 --> 01:34:16.725
because Mark Branch writes a lot of other town regulations

01:34:18.005 --> 01:34:20.405
so he's trying to go there, but

01:34:21.450 --> 01:34:24.090
it just hasn't all sunk into me yet.

01:34:24.890 --> 01:34:26.490
But it's getting a little closer.

01:34:26.890 --> 01:34:31.130
I just hope that Mark Branch doesn't grow frustrated with me as I try to

01:34:31.610 --> 01:34:32.970
make this understandable.

01:34:33.725 --> 01:34:35.085
>> Conceptually,

01:34:35.245 --> 01:34:36.445
like idea

01:34:36.925 --> 01:34:39.405
of three buckets. It makes it easy

01:34:39.805 --> 01:34:52.600
to understand and I think would be fairly easy to enforce as well as you go further on. And I was just wondering about other places We having done might become the model for other places. We could, yep. And

01:34:53.000 --> 01:34:54.120
>> that'd be okay too.

01:34:59.705 --> 01:35:00.505
So

01:35:00.825 --> 01:35:04.585
going back to those temporary signs, I would like to have

01:35:05.465 --> 01:35:09.465
a limit for how long those signs can be up.

01:35:09.945 --> 01:35:12.585
But if political signs go in there, you know, you kinda,

01:35:13.530 --> 01:35:23.770
that takes all that out the window. And there's gotta be a way to do that, I just haven't figured out what it is yet. So that's what I'm struggling with is how to put limits on these temporary signs

01:35:24.410 --> 01:35:27.930
that don't infringe on free speech and get us in trouble. And

01:35:29.525 --> 01:35:31.445
that's at the end of the day where we're at.

01:35:31.925 --> 01:35:35.365
Next part goes on sign construction definitions

01:35:35.365 --> 01:35:36.084
and

01:35:37.765 --> 01:35:38.565
I guess

01:35:40.085 --> 01:35:40.965
canopy,

01:35:41.125 --> 01:35:42.565
you know, flat freestanding,

01:35:42.565 --> 01:35:44.790
those are all kind of straightforward.

01:35:45.110 --> 01:35:46.390
I wrestled with

01:35:46.790 --> 01:35:48.070
mechanical signs.

01:35:53.270 --> 01:35:55.350
Right this minute, it says

01:35:55.670 --> 01:35:58.710
in Andover, we don't have any mechanical signs.

01:35:59.645 --> 01:36:03.085
And I'm looking for some feedback from the Commission on

01:36:06.125 --> 01:36:10.045
do we want the little blow up sign that you see at the tax

01:36:11.565 --> 01:36:15.645
preparer guy has gone crazy or I see him at car lots

01:36:15.860 --> 01:36:21.140
and all that stuff. I don't know that I would see it any place other than the gas stations

01:36:21.620 --> 01:36:24.420
in town. But right this minute,

01:36:24.740 --> 01:36:25.700
my thinking is

01:36:26.340 --> 01:36:35.025
we probably don't need those at Ando. And so I would include that in the definition of mechanical science here, say we're not going to do the forced air

01:36:35.265 --> 01:36:38.145
things that have the blow up guide going around.

01:36:39.985 --> 01:36:42.865
Those are kind of popular. Anybody think we ought to

01:36:43.505 --> 01:36:43.985
have those?

01:36:45.740 --> 01:36:48.300
>> I think you should have a provision for it,

01:36:50.140 --> 01:36:52.860
because at some point it will come up, right?

01:36:53.500 --> 01:36:54.860
>> Well, might,

01:36:56.060 --> 01:36:56.700
it could.

01:36:57.515 --> 01:36:58.235
The

01:36:59.675 --> 01:37:00.955
other thing that

01:37:02.635 --> 01:37:05.355
Mark and I were talking about as we were going through this,

01:37:07.115 --> 01:37:08.315
and there's a lot of

01:37:08.955 --> 01:37:10.075
signs

01:37:10.235 --> 01:37:11.675
that have

01:37:13.870 --> 01:37:15.470
scrolling letters

01:37:15.470 --> 01:37:16.830
and that kind of thing.

01:37:20.030 --> 01:37:21.310
My thought was

01:37:22.670 --> 01:37:24.830
we could have those inside

01:37:27.035 --> 01:37:29.515
is what you put on the inside window

01:37:29.675 --> 01:37:31.115
of your restaurant

01:37:31.115 --> 01:37:31.995
the sign?

01:37:32.395 --> 01:37:34.715
And yes, it is. It is a sign.

01:37:35.595 --> 01:37:40.555
Would we expect somebody to put, you know, I've seen the flashing open signs.

01:37:41.120 --> 01:37:42.000
Okay,

01:37:42.000 --> 01:37:43.920
that's pretty good. I

01:37:44.080 --> 01:37:46.000
don't know that I got heartburn with that.

01:37:47.040 --> 01:37:50.480
I don't want it out on the road because I think it distracts drivers.

01:37:50.960 --> 01:37:54.720
But if you have it back there in the window saying you're open and you want to get somebody's attention,

01:37:55.645 --> 01:37:58.845
I may be okay with that. Looking for

01:37:59.245 --> 01:38:02.685
other thoughts of the commission as well on that.

01:38:04.205 --> 01:38:07.885
>> I think the definition is okay, but calling

01:38:07.885 --> 01:38:09.325
it mechanical

01:38:09.680 --> 01:38:11.840
as a description,

01:38:11.840 --> 01:38:12.560
really

01:38:12.800 --> 01:38:16.240
covers more than mechanical, right? It doesn't have to be mechanical.

01:38:16.240 --> 01:38:17.120
It's really,

01:38:17.360 --> 01:38:21.840
what you're talking about is a dynamic display or an active display

01:38:22.080 --> 01:38:24.320
sign. I think that would be more descriptive

01:38:24.875 --> 01:38:26.155
for a definition.

01:38:28.795 --> 01:38:32.395
>> So say that again, I was getting ready to take a note and my brain

01:38:32.715 --> 01:38:33.115
Yeah,

01:38:33.835 --> 01:38:34.315
mechanical,

01:38:35.275 --> 01:38:37.675
>> if you read the definition of mechanical,

01:38:37.675 --> 01:38:49.350
it really doesn't necessarily have to have any moving mechanical parts, right? Yeah, it can be electronically moving. Yeah, so I would propose we call it active display or dynamic display,

01:38:49.830 --> 01:38:50.390
something

01:38:50.630 --> 01:38:51.830
of that nature.

01:38:52.630 --> 01:38:53.990
Yeah, I like that. Okay.

01:38:57.515 --> 01:38:58.395
Very good.

01:38:59.915 --> 01:39:00.875
>> Go

01:39:00.875 --> 01:39:02.795
back to the temporary Jed.

01:39:03.355 --> 01:39:05.195
There's no time limit on that?

01:39:06.235 --> 01:39:07.435
>> Well, we're not down.

01:39:09.410 --> 01:39:12.130
We'll get there in a few minutes, but there's inconsistencies.

01:39:12.130 --> 01:39:13.250
I don't know how

01:39:14.370 --> 01:39:16.770
we'll get there. We're

01:39:16.770 --> 01:39:19.890
sneaking in on that, but the basic answer is no, no time limits.

01:39:21.475 --> 01:39:23.315
At least I think that if you're gonna,

01:39:24.195 --> 01:39:31.795
your attorney branch is very reluctant to put restrictions on here, anything that says here are the rules for political science,

01:39:32.380 --> 01:39:37.820
because he says that's a red flag for anybody who wants to go challenge it. Why are you putting restrictions on my science?

01:39:38.460 --> 01:39:43.100
But if we include them with other bunch of temporary science, how can we say

01:39:43.500 --> 01:39:48.605
you can do all this for the political one, but you can't do it for the others. So

01:39:50.045 --> 01:39:57.405
I haven't come through the answer to that. We thought we had some things, but it didn't work out and we'll talk about those in a couple of minutes.

01:40:00.845 --> 01:40:02.285
The projecting roof,

01:40:04.690 --> 01:40:07.170
we added something about a sky sign,

01:40:07.170 --> 01:40:11.490
any sign suspended by means of balloon or other than lighter than air device.

01:40:11.890 --> 01:40:15.090
I was concerned about, you know, somebody's going to have

01:40:16.265 --> 01:40:22.025
a signed angler from a drone, but I think that's probably cost prohibitive. I can see you putting the

01:40:22.345 --> 01:40:24.825
little hot air balloon or something to

01:40:24.825 --> 01:40:26.105
hold something up there.

01:40:26.505 --> 01:40:28.745
We certainly can't restrict somebody from

01:40:29.460 --> 01:40:33.620
flying a banner behind an airplane over the town if they were going do that.

01:40:34.020 --> 01:40:34.580
So

01:40:34.900 --> 01:40:35.620
I

01:40:36.100 --> 01:40:41.140
didn't put anything about the drones in there, but we did put in

01:40:43.885 --> 01:40:49.565
that we're going to have a definition of a sky sign and that's what that is.

01:40:51.085 --> 01:40:53.245
And then we added one for the window too,

01:40:55.245 --> 01:40:57.565
and this is where we could

01:40:58.050 --> 01:40:59.490
include something

01:40:59.810 --> 01:41:01.090
about the

01:41:02.050 --> 01:41:04.210
size of a window sign if we wanted.

01:41:04.610 --> 01:41:06.610
I think I'm

01:41:06.610 --> 01:41:11.410
kind of open to, I don't like to put a lot of restrictions on people

01:41:11.815 --> 01:41:13.415
any more than we have to,

01:41:13.815 --> 01:41:16.855
and I'm okay with if it's in the window being the

01:41:17.335 --> 01:41:19.734
scrolling marquee kind of thing or

01:41:19.975 --> 01:41:26.215
the flashing open and that kind of thing. We'd have to work on some of our definitions to include that.

01:41:29.730 --> 01:41:37.970
I'm going to go down to sign lighting right now. Right now we've got two different kinds of lighting. We've got natural lighting, which is sunlight,

01:41:38.530 --> 01:41:39.970
and we've got artificial,

01:41:39.970 --> 01:41:41.570
which is you shine a light on it.

01:41:50.985 --> 01:41:58.505
And it does talk about, you know, like at a gas station, they have the price of gas being

01:41:57.210 --> 01:41:59.050
lit up and that sort of thing. So

01:42:00.330 --> 01:42:06.090
that's where we are there. I'm still working on do we need to expand on that at all and go from there.

01:42:06.730 --> 01:42:08.330
I'll

01:42:08.330 --> 01:42:11.130
probably add to that. Nothing for you guys to consider on that tonight.

01:42:12.975 --> 01:42:14.415
General regulations.

01:42:14.415 --> 01:42:15.135
I thought

